B6 mutation check, 2026-11-11 03:55 UTC
Each mutant injects one bug into a copy of the repository. Mutants of phase_sequencer and sched_pkg run U11
first (+QUICK, then the full run if the short form misses it); the others, and any that U11 misses, rebuild
tb_mesh_c (4x4, 2x2 regions) and run TL01, TL02, TL03, TL04 and TL06 at seed 1, in that order, until one fails.
Every RTL $fatal is turned into $display, so the RTL assertions report but cannot stop the run: only the testbench
(frame_ref, mesh_checker, sched_monitor, router_checker, ni_checker, sinks, scoreboard, idle checks) can kill a
mutant. A survivor is run again with the assertions on. Killed = a run fails (RESULT FAIL, $fatal, hang, or no
RESULT line); the reason is the first error. P02 and M01 were run again alone to print their whole first error.

The first run (03:12 UTC) killed 22 of 24: S10 is equivalent (below), and P02, an epoch sized at k_L = 3, gave the
same power of two as k_L = 4 in every configuration U11 checked. U11 then gained a thirteenth package check, the
epoch on 8x8 with B_MAX 5, where the two differ (2^15 against 2^14), and S13 was added.

